From: arch-lavender <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] layer-shell: do not reject zero-size surfaces without anchors

Phosh 0.57 creates a full-width, bottom-anchored layer surface whose
height is 0.  wlroots 0.20.2 rejects any 0xN or Nx0 layer surface
unless both opposite anchors are set, which makes the phosh home layer
fail to map.

Disable the dimension/anchors validation.  The compositor still sizes
the surface from the anchors later, so this only removes the early
reject.

Upstream source: wlroots 0.20.2.
Apply from the top of the wlroots source tree with:
    patch -p1 < wlroots-0.20.2-layer-shell-0dim.patch
--- a/types/wlr_layer_shell_v1.c
+++ b/types/wlr_layer_shell_v1.c
@@ -358,6 +358,7 @@
 
 	uint32_t anchor = surface->pending.anchor;
 
+#if 0
 	const uint32_t horiz = ZWLR_LAYER_SURFACE_V1_ANCHOR_LEFT |
 		ZWLR_LAYER_SURFACE_V1_ANCHOR_RIGHT;
 	if (surface->pending.desired_width == 0 && (anchor & horiz) != horiz) {
@@ -375,6 +376,7 @@
 			"height 0 requested without setting top and bottom anchors");
 		return;
 	}
+#endif
 
 	if ((anchor & surface->pending.exclusive_edge) != surface->pending.exclusive_edge) {
 		wlr_surface_reject_pending (wlr_surface, surface->resource,